desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Args Os"
	title_zh: "Args Os"
	type: vuln
	level: low
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-args-os"
	risk: "information-exposure"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from rule `args-os` (rust/lang/security/args-os.yml).
Original message: args_os should not be used for security operations. From the docs: "The first element is traditionally the path of the executable, but it can be set to arbitrary text, and might not even exist. This means this property should not be relied upon for security purposes."
CWE: CWE-807: Reliance on Untrusted Inputs in a Security Decision
References:
- https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/env/fn.args_os.html
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review this occurrence and replace it with a safer alternative.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.rs": <<<POS
std::env::args_os()
POS
	"safefile://pos.rs": <<<NEG
std::env::args()
NEG
)

${*.rs}.pattern_regex(/(?:std::env::args_os\(\))/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "low",
	title: "Args Os",
	title_zh: "Args Os",
	message: "Args Os detected.",
}
